.TH GIT-BACKDATE 1 "2025-01-06" "Git External Commands" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-backdate \- Create backdated commits with work hour validation and LLM workflow automation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git backdate what
.br
.B git backdate which
.br
.B git backdate add
.I <file>
[\fI<file>...\fR]
.br
.B git backdate
[\fB--allow-emojis\fR]
[\fB--overtime\fR]
[\fB--detailed\fR]
[\fB--unconventional\fR]
.I <YYYY-MM-DD>
.I <HH:MM>
.I <message>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-backdate
is a Git external command that creates commits with custom backdated timestamps
while enforcing realistic work patterns and conventional commit format.
Designed for LLM agents to maintain organic commit histories through a
state machine workflow.
.PP
This command is discoverable via
.B git help -a
under "External commands".
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B what
Show next action in commit workflow (state machine).
Examines git state and outputs single instruction for LLM.
Auto-initializes repo if needed. After successful commits,
this is called automatically to show next step.
.TP
.B which
Show token-efficient report of untracked and unstaged files.
Outputs file paths with trimmed content for LLM grouping.
Files containing "dont commit" and anachronistic files are excluded.
.TP
.B add
Safely stage files for commit.
Prevents staging files with "dont commit" directives.
Prevents using '.' - requires explicit file listing.
Checks for emojis in text files.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I <YYYY-MM-DD>
Commit date (e.g., 2025-01-15)
.TP
.I <HH:MM>
Commit time (e.g., 09:23)
.TP
.I <message>
Commit message (conventional format, single-line, ASCII only by default)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --overtime
Allow commits outside regular work hours or on weekends
.TP
.B --detailed
Allow multiline commit messages
.TP
.B --unconventional
Allow non-conventional commit message format
.TP
.B --allow-emojis
Allow emojis in code files (applies globally to all subcommands)
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.PP
Note: For multiline unconventional commits, use both
.B --detailed
and
.B --unconventional
.SH COMMIT MESSAGE RULES
.TP
.B 1. ASCII only
Non-ASCII characters are rejected
.TP
.B 2. Single-line by default
Use
.B --detailed
for multiline messages
.TP
.B 3. Conventional format required
(unless
.B --unconventional
):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Format: type(scope): message  OR  type: message
.IP \(bu 2
Valid types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
.IP \(bu 2
Scope: lowercase alphanumeric with hyphens/slashes (optional)
.IP \(bu 2
Examples:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
✓ feat(auth): add login functionality
.IP \(bu 2
✓ fix: resolve parsing bug
.IP \(bu 2
✗ Added new feature (missing type)
.IP \(bu 2
✗ FEAT: something (uppercase type)
.RE
.RE
.SH VALIDATION RULES
.TP
.B 1. Time Sequence
Commits must be at least 1 minute after the last commit
.TP
.B 2. Work Hours
Regular commits allowed 08:00-19:00 (Mon-Fri only). Use
.B --overtime
flag for commits outside these hours or on weekends.
.TP
.B 3. Organic Timing
Minutes cannot be :00, :15, :30, or :45. Valid examples: :07, :23, :38, :52.
Seconds are automatically randomized (1-59).
.TP
.B 4. Staged Files
Files must be staged with
.B git backdate add
before committing
.TP
.B 5. No Emojis
Emojis in text files are rejected unless
.B --allow-emojis
flag is used
.TP
.B 6. Conventional Format
Commit messages must follow conventional format unless
.B --unconventional
flag is used
.SH ANACHRONISTIC FILE DETECTION
Files are automatically excluded to
.B .git/info/exclude
if they are anachronistic (file pattern predates repo timeline):
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B *claude*, .claude/*
- Adoption: 2025-02-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *gemini*, .gemini/*
- Adoption: 2023-12-06
.IP \(bu 2
.B *cursor*, .cursorrules
- Adoption: 2023-06-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *agent*, .agents/*
- Adoption: 2024-01-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *aider*, .aider/*
- Adoption: 2024-01-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *cline*, .cline/*
- Adoption: 2024-06-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *windsurf*, .windsurf/*
- Adoption: 2024-09-01
.IP \(bu 2
.B *copilot*, .github/copilot*
- Adoption: 2021-10-01
.RE
.PP
This ensures backdated commit histories look historically accurate by hiding
references to tools that didn't exist at the time.
.SH LLM WORKFLOW
.TP
.B 1.
Call:
.B git backdate what
.TP
.B 2.
Follow the instruction shown:
.RS
.TP
.B Case A - Staged files exist:
Calculate development time for changes, then execute:
.B git backdate YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM "message"
.br
Script auto-shows next instruction
.TP
.B Case B - Untracked/unstaged changes:
Review report from embedded "git backdate which" output, stage related group with
.B git backdate add <files>,
calculate time and commit. Script auto-shows next instruction.
.TP
.B Case C - Working tree clean:
Job finished, stop
.TP
.B Case D - Merge conflicts:
Abort, return to parent agent
.RE
.TP
.B 3.
Repeat from step 1 (script auto-calls "what" after commits)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
LLM agent workflow:
.RS
.nf
$ git backdate what
Make 1 group of related changes:
UNTRACKED|newfile.js
...
Add with: git backdate add <files>
Commit with: git backdate DATE TIME "message"

$ git backdate add newfile.js utils.js
$ git backdate 2025-01-15 09:23 "feat: add user authentication"
SUCCESS: Commit created successfully!
...
JOB FINISHED: Working tree clean
.fi
.RE
.PP
Manual commit (regular work hour):
.RS
.nf
git backdate 2025-01-15 09:23 "feat: add user authentication"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Manual commit (weekend overtime):
.RS
.nf
git backdate --overtime 2025-01-18 14:17 "fix: critical bug"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Unconventional message:
.RS
.nf
git backdate --unconventional 2025-01-15 10:23 "Add stuff"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Allow emojis in code:
.RS
.nf
git backdate --allow-emojis add emoji-file.js
.fi
.RE
.SH ERRORS
The tool will reject commits that:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Are before or within 1 minute of the last commit
.IP \(bu 2
Use quarter-hour times (:00, :15, :30, :45)
.IP \(bu 2
Are on weekends without --overtime flag
.IP \(bu 2
Are outside 08:00-19:00 without --overtime flag
.IP \(bu 2
Have no staged files
.IP \(bu 2
Contain non-ASCII characters
.IP \(bu 2
Contain newlines (without --detailed)
.IP \(bu 2
Don't follow conventional format (without --unconventional)
.IP \(bu 2
Contain emojis in text files (without --allow-emojis)
.IP \(bu 2
Try to stage files with "dont commit" directive
.IP \(bu 2
Try to use '.' with git backdate add
.RE
.PP
All errors include helpful suggestions for valid alternatives.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .git/info/exclude
Anachronistic files are automatically added here to hide them from version control
while keeping them available locally.
.SH INSTALLATION
Place
.B git-backdate
executable in your PATH (e.g., ~/dotfiles/bin/.local/bin/).
Git will automatically discover it as an external command.
.PP
Verify installation:
.RS
.nf
git help -a | grep backdate
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-add (1),
.BR git-commit (1),
.BR git-log (1)
.PP
Git external commands documentation:
.B git help -a
.PP
Conventional Commits specification:
.B https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
.SH AUTHOR
Created for maintaining organic, historically accurate commit histories with LLM agents.
